  description="The rules for using the PHV Prep UK app, including Premium, your account and acceptable use."
>
  <main class="md:flex md:justify-center">
    <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-[750px]">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: 27 October 2026</em></p>

      <p>
        These Terms of Use ("Terms") explain the rules for using the
        <strong>PHV Prep UK</strong> app ("the app"). The app is run by
        <strong>John Akhis Moreno</strong>, an individual based in the United
        Kingdom ("we", "us"). By creating an account or using the app, you agree
        to these Terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the app.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you downloaded the app from the App Store, Apple's standard Licensed
        Application End User License Agreement also applies. Nothing in these
        Terms limits your rights under it.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What the app is</h2>
      <p>
        PHV Prep UK is an independent study aid for private hire ("taxi badge")
        licensing tests set by the councils listed in the app.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>We are not affiliated with, authorised by, or endorsed by any
        council or licensing authority.</strong> We can't issue licences, book
        tests or process applications.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No guarantee of passing</h2>
      <p>
        The app helps you prepare. It does not guarantee that you will pass any
        test, or that you will be granted a licence. Your result depends on you
        and on the council's own assessment.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Council rules come first</h2>
      <p>
        Councils change their rules, fees, test formats and conditions from time
        to time. We work to keep the app up to date, but our content may
        sometimes lag behind a change. <strong>If anything in the app differs
        from your council's own guidance, the council's guidance is always
        correct.</strong> Check your council's website before you apply or sit a
        test.
      </p>

      <h2>4. The AI Tutor</h2>
      <p>
        The AI Tutor gives automatic answers generated by an AI service provided
        by Anthropic. It can make mistakes, and its answers are <strong>not legal
        advice</strong>. Don't rely on it for decisions about your licence, your
        rights or the law; check with your council or a qualified adviser. How
        the AI Tutor handles your messages is explained in our Privacy Policy.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Premium</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Premium is a one-off purchase</strong>, not a subscription. It
          unlocks Premium for every council in the app, including councils added
          later, for as long as we offer the app. If we ever decide to close the
          app, we'll give you at least 3 months' notice in the app.
        </li>
        <li>
          We won't take away the main things Premium includes: full access to
          the question bank, unlimited mock exams and the higher AI Tutor limit.
        </li>
        <li>
          Payment is taken by <strong>Apple (App Store) or Google (Google
          Play)</strong>, under their terms. We never see your card details.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Refunds and your right to cancel are handled by Apple or
          Google</strong> under their terms and the law. If a purchase is
          refunded, Premium is removed from the account.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can restore Premium on a new device or a new account with
          <strong>"Restore purchase"</strong>, using the same Apple or Google
          account you bought it with.
        </li>
        <li>
          The features of the free version, and its daily limits, may change over
          time.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Your statutory rights are not affected.</strong> Under UK consumer
        law, digital content you pay for must be of satisfactory quality, fit for
        purpose and as described. If Premium is faulty, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:support@yongchivo.com">support@yongchivo.com</a> and we
        will work with you, and with Apple or Google, to put it right.
      </p>
      <p>
        If digital content we supply damages your device or other digital content
        you own, and that happened because we didn't use reasonable care and
        skill, we'll either repair the damage or pay you compensation.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Your account</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You need an account to use the app. Keep your password safe and don't
          share your account with anyone else. You are responsible for what
          happens on your account.
        </li>
        <li>You must be <strong>18 or over</strong> to use the app.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>You can delete your account at any time</strong> in the app: go
          to <strong>Preferences → Delete account</strong> and enter your
          password. What we delete and what we keep is explained in our Privacy
          Policy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You must not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>share your account, or sell or give access to it;</li>
        <li>
          copy, scrape, download in bulk, republish or sell the questions,
          answers, explanations or guides, in any form;
        </li>
        <li>use bots, scripts or other automated tools with the app;</li>
        <li>
          try to get around the daily limits, Premium checks or security
          features;
        </li>
        <li>
          misuse the AI Tutor, for example by trying to make it produce harmful
          or offensive content, using it for purposes unrelated to your exam, or
          sending large volumes of messages automatically;
        </li>
        <li>use the app in any way that breaks the law or harms other people.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Suspending or closing accounts</h2>
      <p>
        We may suspend or close an account if it is used in a serious or repeated
        way that breaks these Terms, for example sharing an account or copying
        the question bank. Where reasonable, we'll tell you first and give you a
        chance to explain. This does not affect your statutory rights.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Our content</h2>
      <p>
        The app's questions, answers, explanations, guides, design and branding
